{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TqEvZUZW9waWPmX1ikPFDJ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Test Writer 2 — Grid.js + AStarFinder + DijkstraFinder\n2\t\n3\t## Scope\n4\tGrid core coverage gaps, AStarFinder constructor/edge-case coverage, DijkstraFinder verification.\n5\t\n6\t---\n7\t\n8\t## Priority 1 — src/core/Grid.js (HIGH)\n9\t\n10\t- `getNeighbors` with `DiagonalMovement.Always` — `d0=d1=d2=d3=true` branch (Grid.js:189)\n11\t- `getNeighbors` with `DiagonalMovement.OnlyWhenNoObstacles` — `d = s3 && s0` branch (Grid.js:180)\n12\t- `getNeighbors` with invalid `diagonalMovement` → should throw `'Incorrect value of diagonalMovement'` (Grid.js:195)\n13\t- `_buildNodes` with mismatched matrix dimensions → should throw `'Matrix size does not fit'` (Grid.js:66)\n14\t- `clone()` — verify cloned grid has identical walkability; mutation of clone doesn't affect original\n15\t- `getNodeAt` — direct test\n16\t- Corner node neighbor pruning (nodes at grid edges where diagonal would be out-of-bounds)\n17\t\n18\t## Priority 2 — src/finders/AStarFinder.js (HIGH)\n19\t\n20\t- Constructor with `allowDiagonal: true` → sets `DiagonalMovement.IfAtMostOneObstacle` + `octile`\n21\t- Constructor with `allowDiagonal: true, dontCrossCorners: true` → sets `DiagonalMovement.OnlyWhenNoObstacles`\n22\t- Constructor with explicit `diagonalMovement` option (all four values)\n23\t- Constructor with custom `heuristic` function\n24\t- Constructor with `weight` != 1 (weighted A*)\n25\t- No-path scenario (start/end isolated by walls) → should return `[]`\n26\t- Start == End (same node)\n27\t- `findPath` — neighbor already in open list with better g-score (`openList.updateItem` branch at AStarFinder.js:116)\n28\t\n29\t## Priority 3 — src/finders/DijkstraFinder.js (MEDIUM)\n30\t\n31\t- Verify heuristic override to `0` — all neighbors explored uniformly\n32\t- No-path scenario → `[]`\n33\t- Constructor option passthrough\n34\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bc0d9080-ce43-40ad-bede-30d07093c04c","uuid":"47b9ad91-2df1-4c53-9499-d4a866f9d56b","timestamp":"2026-04-16T14:01:29.483Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/sagar/template-repo/docs/experiments/001-demo-artifacts/fleets/fleet-01-test-blitz/workers/test-writer-2/input/assignments.md","content":"# Test Writer 2 — Grid.js + AStarFinder + DijkstraFinder\n\n## Scope\nGrid core coverage gaps, AStarFinder constructor/edge-case coverage, DijkstraFinder verification.\n\n---\n\n## Priority 1 — src/core/Grid.js (HIGH)\n\n- `getNeighbors` with `DiagonalMovement.Always` — `d0=d1=d2=d3=true` branch (Grid.js:189)\n- `getNeighbors` with `DiagonalMovement.OnlyWhenNoObstacles` — `d = s3 && s0` branch (Grid.js:180)\n- `getNeighbors` with invalid `diagonalMovement` → should throw `'Incorrect value of diagonalMovement'` (Grid.js:195)\n- `_buildNodes` with mismatched matrix dimensions → should throw `'Matrix size does not fit'` (Grid.js:66)\n- `clone()` — verify cloned grid has identical walkability; mutation of clone doesn't affect original\n- `getNodeAt` — direct test\n- Corner node neighbor pruning (nodes at grid edges where diagonal would be out-of-bounds)\n\n## Priority 2 — src/finders/AStarFinder.js (HIGH)\n\n- Constructor with `allowDiagonal: true` → sets `DiagonalMovement.IfAtMostOneObstacle` + `octile`\n- Constructor with `allowDiagonal: true, dontCrossCorners: true` → sets `DiagonalMovement.OnlyWhenNoObstacles`\n- Constructor with explicit `diagonalMovement` option (all four values)\n- Constructor with custom `heuristic` function\n- Constructor with `weight` != 1 (weighted A*)\n- No-path scenario (start/end isolated by walls) → should return `[]`\n- Start == End (same node)\n- `findPath` — neighbor already in open list with better g-score (`openList.updateItem` branch at AStarFinder.js:116)\n\n## Priority 3 — src/finders/DijkstraFinder.js (MEDIUM)\n\n- Verify heuristic override to `0` — all neighbors explored uniformly\n- No-path scenario → `[]`\n- Constructor option passthrough\n","numLines":34,"startLine":1,"totalLines":34}}}
