{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017nF8oSEiPz9ZJUNfQz6EMg","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t/**\n2\t * @namespace PF.Heuristic\n3\t * @description A collection of heuristic functions.\n4\t */\n5\tmodule.exports = {\n6\t\n7\t  /**\n8\t   * Manhattan distance.\n9\t   * @param {number} dx - Difference in x.\n10\t   * @param {number} dy - Difference in y.\n11\t   * @return {number} dx + dy\n12\t   */\n13\t  manhattan: function(dx, dy) {\n14\t      return dx + dy;\n15\t  },\n16\t\n17\t  /**\n18\t   * Euclidean distance.\n19\t   * @param {number} dx - Difference in x.\n20\t   * @param {number} dy - Difference in y.\n21\t   * @return {number} sqrt(dx * dx + dy * dy)\n22\t   */\n23\t  euclidean: function(dx, dy) {\n24\t      return Math.sqrt(dx * dx + dy * dy);\n25\t  },\n26\t\n27\t  /**\n28\t   * Octile distance.\n29\t   * @param {number} dx - Difference in x.\n30\t   * @param {number} dy - Difference in y.\n31\t   * @return {number} sqrt(dx * dx + dy * dy) for grids\n32\t   */\n33\t  octile: function(dx, dy) {\n34\t      var F = Math.SQRT2 - 1;\n35\t      return (dx < dy) ? F * dx + dy : F * dy + dx;\n36\t  },\n37\t\n38\t  /**\n39\t   * Chebyshev distance.\n40\t   * @param {number} dx - Difference in x.\n41\t   * @param {number} dy - Difference in y.\n42\t   * @return {number} max(dx, dy)\n43\t   */\n44\t  chebyshev: function(dx, dy) {\n45\t      return Math.max(dx, dy);\n46\t  }\n47\t\n48\t};\n49\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bc0d9080-ce43-40ad-bede-30d07093c04c","uuid":"e0b3a44b-7a92-4638-888b-1ba21e4527d2","timestamp":"2026-04-16T14:01:39.866Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/sagar/template-repo/src/core/Heuristic.js","content":"/**\n * @namespace PF.Heuristic\n * @description A collection of heuristic functions.\n */\nmodule.exports = {\n\n  /**\n   * Manhattan distance.\n   * @param {number} dx - Difference in x.\n   * @param {number} dy - Difference in y.\n   * @return {number} dx + dy\n   */\n  manhattan: function(dx, dy) {\n      return dx + dy;\n  },\n\n  /**\n   * Euclidean distance.\n   * @param {number} dx - Difference in x.\n   * @param {number} dy - Difference in y.\n   * @return {number} sqrt(dx * dx + dy * dy)\n   */\n  euclidean: function(dx, dy) {\n      return Math.sqrt(dx * dx + dy * dy);\n  },\n\n  /**\n   * Octile distance.\n   * @param {number} dx - Difference in x.\n   * @param {number} dy - Difference in y.\n   * @return {number} sqrt(dx * dx + dy * dy) for grids\n   */\n  octile: function(dx, dy) {\n      var F = Math.SQRT2 - 1;\n      return (dx < dy) ? F * dx + dy : F * dy + dx;\n  },\n\n  /**\n   * Chebyshev distance.\n   * @param {number} dx - Difference in x.\n   * @param {number} dy - Difference in y.\n   * @return {number} max(dx, dy)\n   */\n  chebyshev: function(dx, dy) {\n      return Math.max(dx, dy);\n  }\n\n};\n","numLines":49,"startLine":1,"totalLines":49}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01QPgW8nfV5GkpspdMY5eCN8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have enough info. Let me create the test files. I'll write two test files:\n1. `test/Grid.coverage.js` - extending Grid coverage (since I cannot modify existing Grid.js tests)\n2. `test/AStarFinder.js` - new file for AStarFinder tests\n3. `test/DijkstraFinder.js` - new file for DijkstraFinder tests\n\nLet me plan all the tests needed:\n\n**Grid coverage (test/Grid.coverage.js)**:\n1. `getNeighbors` with `DiagonalMovement.Always` — all d0..d3=true → includes diagonals regardless of walls\n\n\n2. `getNeighbors` with `DiagonalMovement.OnlyWhenNoObstacles` — d = s3 && s0 (both sides must be walkable)\n3. `getNeighbors` with invalid diagonalMovement → throw 'Incorrect value of diagonalMovement'\n4. `_buildNodes` with mismatched matrix dimensions → throw 'Matrix size does not fit'\n5. `clone()` — identical walkability, mutation isolation\n6. `getNodeAt` — direct test\n7. Corner node neighbor pruning — at edges, diagonals out-of-bounds are not returned\n\n**AStarFinder (test/AStarFinder.js)**:\n1. Constructor with various options...\n2. Constructor with `allowDiagonal: true, dontCrossCorners: true` → OnlyWhenNoObstacles\n3. Constructor with explicit `diagonalMovement` — all four values\n4. Constructor with custom heuristic function\n5. Constructor with `weight: 2` (weighted A*)\n6. No-path scenario → []\n7. Start == End → returns path of 1 element or 0 (need to test)\n8. `openList.updateItem` branch — neighbor already in open list with better g-score\n\nNow I'm checking the start==end case. Looking at the A* implementation, when start and end are the same node, it gets initialized with g=0 and f=0, then pushed to the open list. I need to verify what the actual path output is in this edge case.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"